If you have downloaded a binary package of FIRE, 
it might work for you without any installation.
However, the prefferred way to install FIRE is 
to get it from git and build from sources.

------------- Short installation version -------------
$ git clone git@bitbucket.org:feynmanIntegrals/fire.git
$ cd fire/FIRE7
$ sudo apt-get update -y
$ sudo apt-get install -y cln-dev
$ sudo apt-get install -y ginac-tools
$ sudo apt-get install -y libginac-dev
$ ./configure 
$
# Now read the options provided by ./configure and reconfigure with desired options, for example: 
# $ ./configure --enable_zlib --enable_snappy --enable_tcmalloc --enable_zstd
$ make dep
$ make
------------- /Short installation version -------------


------------- Installation version with explanations -------------
git clone git@bitbucket.org:feynmanIntegrals/fire.git

cd fire/FIRE7
./configure

You can read the options provided by ./configure and reconfigure with desired options

The prerequesities to build FIRE are
- cln
For install cln library (CLN - Class Library for Numbers):
sudo apt-get update -y
sudo apt-get install -y cln-dev

- ginac
For install GiNaC library:
sudo apt-get install -y ginac-tools
sudo apt-get install -y libginac-dev

- pari
sudo apt-get install -y bison

- kyotocabinet
- lz4 (or other Data Compression Library like Snappy, or ZStandard, or Zlib)
to use another Data Compression library you can ./configure with options like --enable-snappy. The default library is lz4.

The package comes with proper versions of kyotocabinet and lz4.
(in the extra folder)
So if you do not have them installed, run

make dep

The libraries are compiled and "installed" in the usr subfolder

------------- snappy compilation errors -------------  
If there is something wrong with snappy compilation (libtool version)

libtool: Version mismatch error.  This is libtool 2.4.2 
Debian-2.4.2-1ubuntu1, but the
libtool: definition of this LT_INIT comes from libtool 2.2.6b.
libtool: You should recreate aclocal.m4 with macros from libtool 2.4.2 
Debian-2.4.2-1ubuntu1
libtool: and run autoconf again.

the solution is to run

cd extra/snappy-1.1.1/
autoreconf -fvi
cd ../..
------------- /snappy compilation errors -------------

Then just run

make

To get the latest version of FIRE, run

git pull
make

------------- /Installation version with explanations -------------

------------- How to make clean rebuild -------------
In case of changes in ./configure options it is recommended to have a clean rebuild

make cleandep
make clean
./configure
make dep
make

------------- /How to make clean rebuild -------------

------------- Libs -------------
- apt-get update
- apt-get install -y g++
- apt-get install -y make
- apt-get install -y cmake
- apt-get install -y zlib1g-dev
- apt-get install -y doxygen
- apt-get install -y libcln-dev
- apt-get install -y libginac-dev
------------- /Libs -------------
